Proposed upstream fix for PreprocessPipeline (yoshihito-saito/PreprocessPipeline, observed at commit cb89e24, 2026-09-02).
NOT applied to the local checkout; ephys/run_sort_session.py works around it at runtime (_install_ks4_partition_shim).

Symptom: sorter=kilosort4 with sorter_partition_mode="shank" (or "probe") fails in every partition with
    IndexError: Channel '16' was not in probe['chanMap']
    (kilosort/io.py remove_bad_channels, called from spikeinterface/sorters/external/kilosort4.py _run_from_folder)

Cause: execute_sorting_job() sets params["bad_channels"] = ignored_channels_0based (full-recording indices) and then
reduces the recording to the partition's channel subset via select_recording_channels(); spikeinterface's Kilosort4
wrapper builds probe["chanMap"] = np.arange(n_chan) over that subset, so the full-width indices cannot be found.
In the subset case the ignored channels are already removed from the recording, so bad_channels must not be passed.

--- a/src/preprocess/sorter_runner.py
+++ b/src/preprocess/sorter_runner.py
@@ -1897,8 +1897,12 @@ def execute_sorting_job(
         with _kilosort4_package_override(kilosort4_import_root):
             _KILOSORT4_ALLOWED_PARAM_KEYS = None
             params = _normalize_kilosort4_params(params)
-        if ignored_channels_0based:
+        # When the sorter input is a channel SUBSET (probe/shank partition) the ignored channels are already
+        # removed by select_recording_channels() below and spikeinterface's Kilosort4 wrapper numbers the subset
+        # 0..n-1, so full-recording indices in bad_channels raise "Channel 'k' was not in probe['chanMap']".
+        # Pass bad_channels only for full-width input.
+        if ignored_channels_0based and not sorter_uses_channel_subset:
             params["bad_channels"] = ignored_channels_0based
         print("Resolved Kilosort4 params")
     params = _merge_sorter_job_kwargs(params, job_kwargs)
